# Shell scripts and configs are executed on Linux. A CR at end of line makes bash
# fail with `$'\r': command not found` and mangles `case`/`set` parsing, so these
# MUST be stored and checked out with LF regardless of the committer's platform.
#
# This bit us: scripts authored on Windows were committed with CRLF and every
# script in the repo was unrunnable on the VPS.
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.py        text eol=lf
*.toml      text eol=lf
*.conf      text eol=lf
*.service   text eol=lf
*.md        text eol=lf
*.txt       text eol=lf
*.example   text eol=lf
